      "notes": "Population PK/PD parameters, P. aeruginosa pneumonia model (plasma and ELF)\nS06 | DOI 10.1128/aac.01559-10 | Table 2 (Drusano et al. 2011)\nNeutropenic female Swiss-Webster mice 24-26 g (cyclophosphamide 150 mg/kg day -4 and 100 mg/kg day -1 i.p.); intranasal P. aeruginosa PAO1 2 × 10^7 CFU. PK: single i.p. doses spanning 2.4-150 mg/kg given to four groups 5 h after inoculation (individual doses not listed); 11 times over 0-5 h, 2-3 mice per time; plasma and urea-corrected BAL (ELF) by LC-MS/MS.\nEfficacy: \"Five animal cohorts were administered meropenem i.p. at doses of 50, 100, 150, 200, 300, and 450 mg/kg every 4 h\" (five cohorts but six doses, as printed) from 5 h after inoculation; lungs harvested 24 h after the start of therapy. Mice per cohort not stated; 5 mice killed for baseline counts.\nConcentrations are in Figs. 1-2 only (not transcribed). Vc/F and CL/F are per animal (liters, liters/h), not per kg. Protein binding not reported. Table read once from the journal HTML.\nText: ELF penetration about 40% (median 39%); exposure targets \"31.7%, 49.6%, and 49.8% of the dosing interval\" time > MIC in ELF (abstract: 32%, 50%, 50%); endpoint mapping (2-log kill, 3-log kill, resistance suppression) paraphrased, NOT_VERIFIED. Strain MIC 0.5 to 1.0 mg/L.",
